 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? The standard height for a monitor on a desk is about ear level when sitting. Some people like the top of the monitor just below eye level. A typical monitor is about half a metre away. Some people use it further back, some closer, depending on your eye sight. A laptop is different. Many people use it at eye level, either on the desk or on their lap. Textbooks are fine for reading, just not for long at a time. A good rule is no book closer than an arm's length.",
